1
00:00:00,820 --> 00:00:02,999
May, 1967.

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:06,295
A thin jet climbs into the night above
Thailand.

3
00:00:06,730 --> 00:00:12,493
No markings. No bombs. Just a pilot, a camera,
and two long cases in its belly.

4
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:16,724
The pilot is Chuang. His unit is called the
Black Cats.

5
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:21,059
Made by the CIA and Taiwan, the Black Cats fly
the U-2.

6
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:24,631
A jet with the wings of a glider, near the
edge of space.

7
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:27,725
China is about to test a hydrogen bomb.

8
00:00:28,170 --> 00:00:31,927
Satellites can photograph the desert. But they
cannot feel it.

9
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:40,765
So Chuang will fly three thousand kilometers,
cross the bamboo curtain, and drop two
listening posts into the sand near Lop Nur.

10
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:44,143
Each one is two meters long. It lands, and
waits.

11
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,787
If the earth moves, it will tell Taipei.

12
00:00:47,280 --> 00:00:51,827
On June seventeenth, a bomb called six three
nine falls from an H-6.

13
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,701
Three point three megatons.

14
00:00:55,970 --> 00:00:58,251
Six weeks later, the sensors answer.

15
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:01,119
The signal is small. The meaning is not.

16
00:01:02,070 --> 00:01:07,918
The flights end in 1974. The planes go home.
The desert keeps the rest.
